<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<div style=""><font face="arial"><b>Dear Client</b>,</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">Employees can make changes to their Insperity Group Health Plan coverage during their annual open enrollment period. If no changes are made during open enrollment, the employee’s current election — including an election of no coverage — will carry over to the next coverage period. If a coverage option is discontinued and no new election is made, employees will be moved to the closest comparable option at the new rates for their coverage tier.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><b>Changes Outside Open Enrollment</b></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><b><br></b></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">After open enrollment ends, employees may only change their elections if they experience a <b>Qualifying Life Event (QLE)</b>. Employees have <b>60 days from the event date</b> to request a change.<br><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><b>Examples of Qualifying Life Events include:<br><br></b></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Marriage, divorce, or legal separation</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Beginning or ending a domestic partnership</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Birth, adoption, or placement for adoption</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Death of a dependent</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Change in dependent or employee eligibility under another group health plan</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Court order requiring coverage (QMCSO)</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Change in residence that affects eligibility</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Gaining or losing eligibility for Medicare, Medicaid, or CHIP</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Enrollment in Marketplace coverage</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Reduction in hours (less than 30 per week) with enrollment in other coverage</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span>Other events permitted by the Plan<br><br></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><b>Important:<br><br></b></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span><b>Enrollments and additions</b> (e.g., adding a spouse or newborn) are generally <b>retroactive to the event date</b> if requested within 60 days.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">•<span style="white-space:pre">	</span><b>Terminations</b> are usually <b>prospective</b> (effective when the request is submitted), except for <b>death, divorce, or domestic partnership termination</b>, which remain retroactive.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><b>How to Submit a Mid-Year Change:</b></font></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>